   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br>Hello Dr. Chalmers,<br><br><br>Using random slope parameters, I generated some data using <a href=\"https://www.rdocumentation.org/packages/mirt/versions/1.27.1/topics/simdata\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.rdocumentation.org/packages/mirt/versions/1.27.1/topics/simdata&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792473677652000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3OlH_udu96ix1IU1cw-AfG\">simdata</a>. I can recover estimates of these parameters using the <a href=\"https://rdrr.io/cran/mirt/man/coef-method.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://rdrr.io/cran/mirt/man/coef-method.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792473677652000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0xe_ZlRZEXAajgE2AmARza\">coef-method</a> on a model obtained from running the <a href=\"https://www.rdocumentation.org/packages/mirt/versions/1.27.1/topics/mirt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.rdocumentation.org/packages/mirt/versions/1.27.1/topics/mirt&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792473677652000&amp;usg=AOvVaw21lE_QX3YH7gMxmFNzyD5H\">mirt</a> function on the data.<br><br>I&#39;d just like to know if the order of estimated slope parameters matches that of the &quot;true&quot; parameters used to simulated the data.<br><br>For example, given a slope matrix <font face=\"courier new,monospace\">a<font face=\"arial,sans-serif\"> with two factors:<br></font></font><br><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:10pt!important;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap!important;line-height:15px;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:-webkit-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">            [,1]      [,2]\r\n [1,] 1.08624628 1.3448732\r\n [2,]     ...       ...<br><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\"><br>Do a1,a2 in the output of coef-method correspond to column 1,2 of the</span><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\"> <font face=\"courier new,monospace\">a<font face=\"arial,sans-serif\"> </font></font>matrix respectively?</span><br><br>$Item_1\r\n       a1    a2      d g u\r\npar 1.318 1.369 -1.205 0 1<span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\"><br><br>Or is the order not preserved, only the magnitudes?<br><br><br><br>Thanks kindly in advance for your attention,<br>David</span><br></pre></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
